# CODEOWNERS — require owner review for the agent operating system + security controls.
#
# WHY: rule 54 (.claude/rules/54-untrusted-external-content.md) — the real risk from a public
# `.claude/` is INTEGRITY (a poisoned PR weakening the rules/hooks/scanner), not confidentiality.
# Assigning these paths to the owner means any change to them needs the owner's review.
#
# ENFORCEMENT: this file only takes effect when the default branch's protection rule has
# **"Require review from Code Owners"** enabled (Settings → Branches → branch protection — a repo
# setting only the owner can toggle). The agent runs under the owner's credentials, so this gates
# EXTERNAL contributors, not the owner's own agent-driven merges.

# --- the agent operating system: binding rules, enforcement hooks, skills, commands, crons ---
/.claude/                                   @lllyys
/AGENTS.md                                  @lllyys
/CLAUDE.md                                  @lllyys

# --- the untrusted-content security controls (scanner + canary) ---
/scripts/scan-untrusted-content.sh          @lllyys
/scripts/injection-canary-test.sh           @lllyys

# --- CI / automation supply chain (if/when GitHub Actions are added) ---
/.github/                                   @lllyys

# --- release / version / build config (publishing path — worker ≠ publisher) ---
/project.yml                                @lllyys
/android/version.properties                 @lllyys
/scripts/run-tests.sh                       @lllyys
/scripts/run-android-tests.sh               @lllyys
/scripts/run-android-verify.sh              @lllyys
/scripts/run-codex.sh                       @lllyys
